.TH geectl-pull-request-search 1  "geectl-pull-request-search 0.3.0" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-pull\-request\-search \- Search pull requests: OBS submit requests and Gitea pull requests as one list, OBS first then Gitea. With no `\-\-backend` both arms run; `\-\-backend` scopes to one
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl pull\-request search\fR [\fB\-\-backend\fR] [\fB\-\-state\fR] [\fB\-\-creator\fR] [\fB\-\-reviewer\fR] [\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Search pull requests: OBS submit requests and Gitea pull requests as one list, OBS first then Gitea. With no `\-\-backend` both arms run; `\-\-backend` scopes to one
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-backend\fR \fI<BACKEND>\fR
Only this backend (`obs` or `gitea`). With no backend both arms run, OBS first then Gitea
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
obs
.IP \(bu 2
gitea
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fI<STATE>\fR
Only pull requests in these unified states. With none given each arm applies its own default (new/review/declined on OBS, open on Gitea). A state an arm in scope cannot produce is refused: `closed` is never produced by OBS, and no Gitea pull request can ever be `declined`, `withdrawn`, `superseded`, or `deleted` — scope the search with `\-\-backend` to use those
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
open
.IP \(bu 2
merged
.IP \(bu 2
declined
.IP \(bu 2
withdrawn
.IP \(bu 2
closed
.IP \(bu 2
superseded
.IP \(bu 2
deleted
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-creator\fR \fI<CREATOR>\fR
Only pull requests by this author
.TP
\fB\-\-reviewer\fR \fI<REVIEWER>\fR
Only pull requests with review requested of this login. On Gitea, only the token owner\*(Aqs login: the server filters review requests for the authenticated user only. On OBS, an open review addressed to the login
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<REPO>\fR
Only pull requests in this Gitea repo (`owner/repo`). Requires `\-\-backend gitea`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
